<title>USA: Canada takes major share of U.S. 1996 beef imports.</title>
<headline>Canada takes major share of U.S. 1996 beef imports.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-02-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canada replaced Australia as the top supplier of beef to the U.S. market in 1996, U.S. Agriculture Department said Wednesday.</p>
<p>Canadian beef exports to the U.S. last year totaled 227,693 tonnes while Australia beef exports were 182,881 tonnes, according to customs data, USDA said. By comparison, in 1995, Australia exported 216,914 tonnes to the U.S. and Canada exported 167,883 tonnes.</p>
<p>USDA said Australia looked for alternative markets for its beef due to large supplies of cow meat in the U.S. market and tight supplies of high quality beef. At the same time, Canada liquidated its beef herd in 1996 and upped U.S. exports.</p>
